---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const effective = 'September 3, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms for the Identizen hosted services: the public index, the dashboard, the iOS app, and the documentation."
>
  <div class="container-site max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-24">
    <article class="prose-idz">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Effective {effective}</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">
        These terms cover the services Identizen operates: the public index at index.identizen.com,
        the dashboard at app.identizen.com, the Identizen app, and this website and its
        documentation. By using them you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>
        The Identizen software is open source under the Apache License 2.0 and is provided as is,
        without warranty. A deployment you run yourself is governed by that license alone, not by
        these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>The hosted services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The public index is offered free of charge for personal identities. We aim to keep it
          available but do not guarantee availability, and we may change or discontinue it with
          reasonable notice posted on this site and in the app.
        </li>
        <li>
          Sites may register with the public index to accept Identizen sign-ins. Site operators are
          responsible for their own users, content, and compliance.
        </li>
        <li>
          Enterprise customers receive the availability, support, and data-processing commitments in
          their order form and data-processing agreement, which take precedence over these terms
          where they conflict.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use the services to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>attack, probe, or overload the services or any site that uses them;</li>
        <li>
          impersonate another person or site, or send sign-in requests to people who did not ask for
          them;
        </li>
        <li>register sites for phishing, fraud, or the distribution of malware;</li>
        <li>circumvent rate limits, revocation, or any other security control.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may disable sites, devices, or identities that we reasonably believe are doing so.</p>

      <h2>Your identity</h2>
      <p>
        Your private keys and recovery phrase exist only on your devices and in your own records. We
        cannot recover a lost recovery phrase for a personal identity and cannot sign in as you. You
        are responsible for keeping your phone and recovery phrase secure. Sites keep their own
        account-recovery paths.
      </p>

      <h2>The app</h2>
      <p>
        The Identizen app is licensed to you for use on Apple devices you own or control, under
        Apple's standard licensed application end user license agreement in addition to these terms.
        Apple is not responsible for the app or its content and has no obligation to provide support
        for it.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        How we handle data is described in the <a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, which
        forms part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The hosted services are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
        express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
        non-infringement. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any
        indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data,
        profits, or business, arising from your use of the services. Our total liability for any
        claim relating to the free services is limited to one hundred US dollars. Some jurisdictions
        do not allow these limitations, in which case they apply to the extent permitted.
      </p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using the services at any time and remove your identity from your devices. We
        may suspend or terminate access for breach of these terms. Sections that by their nature
        should survive termination do so.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We will post material changes here with a new effective date and, for enterprise customers,
        notify the account contact. Continued use after the effective date is acceptance of the
        changed terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>legal@identizen.com</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
